<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  TruvioCommerce/PimWorkspace.query — the query that backs the Dynamic Workspace
  "Truvio PIM - by data model" (DynamicStructures 100170; this file's Id GUID is what
  DynamicStructureQueryId names, and the two move together or the workspace opens empty).

  WHY THIS LAYER SHIPS A REPOSITORY FILE AT ALL
  A Dynamic Workspace is a PROJECTION, not storage: it is a backing query plus level
  definitions. The rows that define it (DynamicStructures, DynamicStructureLevels) are
  sample-data rows, so the query they point at ships in the same layer — query and rows
  arrive together or neither is useful. It lands in the TruvioCommerce repository that
  surface-swift already owns, beside Products.index, which is the index it sources.

  WHY IT IS NOT Products.query
  Products.query is the STOREFRONT query. It resolves Dynamicweb.Ecommerce.Context macros
  (LanguageID, ShopID) that exist only on a server-rendered storefront request. A workspace
  runs in the BACKEND, where those macros resolve to nothing and the query silently matches
  nothing, so this file states its language as a constant and names no shop at all: the
  workspace's shop scope comes from the DATAMODEL_Truvio_PIM level, not from a predicate.

  THE PREDICATE, AND WHY EACH PART IS HERE
    LanguageID = ENU   one document per product, not one per language. A level counts index
                       DOCUMENTS under this predicate, so without it every node count is
                       multiplied by the language fan-out and the level sum overshoots the
                       query total. Narrow the query, never the level.
    IsVariant = False   masters only. The catalogue ships 36 variant rows beside its 60
                       masters; a workspace that lists both makes the enrichment worklist
                       read as 97 items of work where there are 61.
  There is deliberately NO Active filter: a PIM workbench must show the product that is
  not live yet, which is exactly the product that still needs enriching.

  LEVEL SOURCES (in DynamicStructureLevels, not here) are both NON-ANALYSED keyword fields:
  DATAMODEL_Truvio_PIM (emitted only when the Products.index Full build carries
  SkipDataModels=False) then GroupNames. An analysed free-text field would enumerate
  lower-cased Lucene term fragments and a numeric field would enumerate nodes that open onto
  zero rows; neither errors, so the check is the SUM of the node counts against this query's
  own total.

  COMPLETENESS. CompletionRules is deliberately EMPTY. The completeness percentage a product
  editor shows comes from the QUERY's rule list, so a consumer that wants it adds the four
  rule ids (100160-100163) and CompletionLanguages ENU here. Know what that costs before you
  do: the helper's AppendCompletionExpressions default IS the "Exclude products with 100%
  completeness" checkbox, so a rule list turns this workspace into a worklist of INCOMPLETE
  products rather than the whole catalogue.
-->
<Query ID="5d8e3b27-91a4-4c6f-b0d2-7ae15f43c908" Name="PimWorkspace.query">
  <Meta />
  <Settings />
  <Parameters />
  <Source Repository="TruvioCommerce" Item="Products.index" Type="Dynamicweb.Indexing.Queries.IndexQueryProvider, Dynamicweb.Core" />
  <SortOrder>
    <Sort Field="NameForSort" Direction="Ascending" />
  </SortOrder>
  <Expressions>
    <GroupExpression Operator="And">
      <BinaryExpression Operator="Equal" Disabled="false">
        <Left>
          <FieldExpression Field="LanguageID" />
        </Left>
        <Right>
          <ConstantExpression Value="ENU" Type="System.String" />
        </Right>
      </BinaryExpression>
      <BinaryExpression Operator="Equal" Disabled="false">
        <Left>
          <FieldExpression Field="IsVariant" />
        </Left>
        <Right>
          <ConstantExpression Value="False" Type="System.Boolean" />
        </Right>
      </BinaryExpression>
    </GroupExpression>
  </Expressions>
  <ViewFields />
  <ViewLanguages />
  <Meta />
  <CompletionRules />
  <CompletionLanguages />
  <ListViewFields />
</Query>
